    "question": {
      ":question/id": "4915d23e-2dfb-51b3-a532-f60bf710473e",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following are **not** autonomous ordinary differential equations?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2=4\\left(x^{2}\\right)$\n- **II.** $y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2=4\\left(\\sin{\\left(y \\right)}\\right)$\n- **III.** $y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2=4\\left(y^{2}\\right)$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "An ordinary differential equation with dependent variable $y$ and independent variable $x$ is said to be autonomous if it can be written in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y),$ or equivalently, ${y}^{\u2032}=f(y).$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each of the differential equations:\n\n- Equation I is not an autonomous differential equation. If we isolate the derivative term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2 & =4\\left(x^{2}\\right) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{4\\left(x^{2}\\right)-2}{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)=4 x - \\frac{2}{x}.$ So, it is not possible to write the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y).$\n\n- Equation II is an autonomous differential equation. Writing the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2 & =4\\left(\\sin{\\left(y \\right)}\\right) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{4\\left(\\sin{\\left(y \\right)}\\right)-2}{y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =f(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(y)=\\frac{2 \\left(2 \\sin{\\left(y \\right)} - 1\\right)}{y}.$\n\n- Equation III is an autonomous differential equation. Writing the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2 & =4\\left(y^{2}\\right) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{4\\left(y^{2}\\right)-2}{y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =f(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(y)=4 y - \\frac{2}{y}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "4d20310e-6da8-5c3f-a167-aa4ed6076206",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
